{
  "slug": "claim-swaps-staked-drainer-2024-11",
  "kind": "wallet-drainer",
  "title": "claim::swapS drainer kit: staked SUI, lending and LP positions taken by switching shared state after signature, November and December 2024",
  "network": "mainnet",
  "summary": "A wallet signed a gas-sponsored PTB (F3TCZ6Ki, 19:03:29 UTC on 28 November 2024) that passed its three StakedSui objects, its SUI coin and its sSUI coin into claim::swapS and claim::swapT of package 0xa032d8b8 and minted it 8,314 of a bait coin (CTX). swapS withdraws each stake and pays profit_split percent (75) of it to one collector (0x55abfb40) and the rest to a second (0x532517d0), so 693.41 SUI ($2.41K) left the signer. The package's shared ClaimParams was created with initialized false and zero amounts, which makes every call hand the signer's objects back, and its owner rewrote the amounts and called set_claimable(true) 0.935 s before the drain executed, so a dry run at signing showed no loss. The same kit, re-published from fresh publishers minutes before each large drain and paying the same two collectors, took Suilend obligations, Cetus, Turbos and Bluefin positions and an AlphaFi receipt through swapN, which sends objects whole to 0x532517d0; that address forwarded about 95 of them to operator wallets that unwound them. The first collector was first funded by the second, and the gas sponsor 0xd1c052a8 paid gas for 767 distinct addresses.",
